      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Having other data could be useful as well, like the number of people in the instance, the instance soft cap, and the instance type (imagine being able to make an avatar public with some of those nice animations people like that are a nuisance in public worlds, but being able to restrict the animation to non-public instances). \nIt'd also be useful to be able to get local date/time -- you could actually have a functioning watch, and effects that are only active at certain times of day or on certain days.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-02-15T10:08:56.416Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Providing a default parameter for notifications (like the existing MuteSelf parameter) would allow content creators to make things like wearable smart devices (watches, glasses) or create custom HUD elements while still having full functionality of the existing notification system. This parameter could be in the form of a simple boolean (hasNotification=true/false) or an int specifying how many active notifications the user has (0=none, 1=1 notification, etc.). \n\nAdditionally, this could also be a more robust feature by specifying the type of the most recent notification with an additional int (0=friend, 1=invite, 2=invReq, etc). Doing so would help expand this feature for creators to make more personal, customizable elements for their avatars.",
